{
  "_about": "EV-013 cases for plan kensaku-v1-1 (product image selection). urlCases test rule I1 (URL eligibility, no network); selectionCases test rule I2 (which product pages may supply an image, and in what order) on real Exa responses; bytesCases test rule I3 (what the image proxy accepts after fetching) on the type and dimensions measured by spikes/exa-v1-1/image-probe.mjs on 2026-11-21, plus synthetic edge cases. Image bytes are not committed.",
  "labelStatus": "Assistant-proposed labels computed by a reference implementation of the written rules in docs/futari/ARCHITECTURE.md 'Product images' (independent of src/), checked by hand. They become gold labels only when the owner approves plan kensaku-v1-1. Whether an image shows the right product is not decidable by these rules; EV-016's owner image audit measures it.",
  "rules": {
    "I1": "An image URL is eligible only if it is at most 2048 characters, parses, uses http or https, has no username or password, and its last path segment (percent-decoded, lowercased) neither ends in '.svg' nor contains any of: logo, social, share, placeholder, missing, noimage, no-image, no_image, sprite, banner, campaign, brandimage, uedata, pixel, spacer, favicon, 1x1.",
    "I2": "For one product, consider that product's search hits in Exa result order. A hit can supply its image only if the image URL passes I1 and the hit is (tier 1) a merchant offer in the selected market's currency, else (tier 2) on a manufacturer host and classified as a merchant offer or as evidence not-a-listing or merchant-no-price, else (tier 3) any other merchant offer. A manufacturer host is one whose labels (hostname split on '.' and '-') include the candidate brand normalized with NFKC, lowercased, and stripped of non-letters and non-digits, when that brand has at least 3 characters. Aggregator, editorial, marketplace, search-or-category, merchant-mismatch and rejected hits never supply images. Order: tier 1, then 2, then 3, each in Exa order; drop repeated image URLs; keep at most 4.",
    "I3": "After fetching (see ARCHITECTURE 'Image proxy'), the bytes are accepted only if they are at most 5 MiB, their magic bytes identify JPEG, PNG, WebP or AVIF, both pixel dimensions are known, the shorter side is at least 200 px, and width/height is between 0.5 and 2.0 inclusive."
  },
